      "content": "The belief in perfect oversight is a comforting illusion that ignores the systemic nature of power. Once a surveillance infrastructure is built, the temptation for mission creep—using security tools for social control—is virtually guaranteed, regardless of initial good intentions. The tangible benefits of convenience pale in comparison to the irreversible erosion of civil liberties that mass biometric tracking represents for an entire population.",
      "source": "target",
